.TH SHUFFLE 6.SH NAMEshuffle \- a switch puzzle.SH SYNOPSIS\fBshuffle\fR[\-L level].SH DESCRIPTIONA full-screen puzzle: a row of numbered switches, and flipping one flipsits neighbours too.  It asks\fBWich switch ?\fRand counts your moves; get them all the same way.\fBq\fRquits.\fB\-L\fRstarts at a harder level.  It wants TERM set..PPFor shuffling lines of text, use\fBsort \-r\fRor\fBtac\fR.\fR